  "summary": "One native run of NAT-022 canary-trig-fault (RECOVERY image sha256 e7ab288fdd689dcb15c58cf92e19a96586b30ec3b85a6df09695d3b41772a735, canary Image f839ba305fae5e89c48642b422a827bc4993d491681560b2b20fd1a46b560a1b, source commit 2e0e195). It was written to RECOVERY (/dev/block/sda18) with a matching full readback and booted once (adb reboot recovery at 2026-11-10T13:43:48Z). The owner filmed the screen; decode_video.py decoded 581 CRC-valid frames (4.2-63.9 s of the 66 s recording; the screen is dark from about 64.9 s). First round (canary loop): CHECK 0xA5A5, ENTRY 0x8900 (EL2, MMU off, D-cache off, I-cache on), BOOTID 0x4FEE1585 (differs from run 002 0x1AE1D195), STAGE 0x10, 10 REG frames of the DECON0 kick (status 2 = SW form, GLOBAL_CON 0x113, TRIG_CON 0x3063->0x3062, FRAME_COUNT 165->315, kick 6). Then STAGE 0x11 (about to BRK), then the exception loop: SLOT 4 (BRK at EL2 with SPx), ESR 0x00000000f2001234 (EC 0x3c, ISS 0x1234), ELR 0x00000000801a2fb8, FAR 0x5efe5e5c70ff25fc, then REG (status 2, GLOBAL_CON 0x113, TRIG_CON 0x3063->0x3062, FRAME_COUNT 1967->2117, kick count 14) and the SLOT/ESR/ELR cycle repeating. The Image holds exactly one BRK #0x1234 word (0xd4224680), at file offset 0x2fb8; the decoded ELR therefore implies the Image was executing at 0x801a0000. FAR is architecturally UNKNOWN for BRK and is not an address. The exception-entry STAGE 0x1f frame is replaced at once (no dwell) and was not visible. Stock RECOVERY was restored with one NAT-013 session in Download Mode (bus 5 dev 51, 2026-11-10T13:46:31Z entry); full hash equals stock 96620b8b…, check_android pass, Android booted.",
